      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the original test. The key observations are:\n1. Only `consumeEscapedId()` is actually annotated with `@Test` — the other 7 methods are unused dead code\n2. The test body lacks comments explaining the escape sequences being tested\n3. Removing dead code and adding clear explanations will greatly improve understandability\n\nLet me write the improved test.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the 7 unused dead-code methods (stream providers and unused helpers that had no `@Test` or `@ParameterizedTest` annotations) and adds a class-level Javadoc plus inline comments that explain the escape sequence semantics, making it immediately clear what each assertion verifies."
